      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Anatomía empírica de estimadores de Offline Policy Evaluation (OPE)\"\n",
        "lang: es\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "jupyter: python3\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "Se define el valor de una política $\\pi : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\Delta(\\mathcal{A})$ como la recompensa esperada bajo la política $\\pi$:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "V^{\\pi} = \\mathbb{E}_{\\pi} [R] = \\mathbb{E}[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)]\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "donde $\\mu(X,a) := \\mathbb{E}[R|X,A=a]$ es la recompensa esperada condicionada al contexto  \n",
        "$X \\in \\mathcal{X}$ y a la acción $A=a$, y $\\Delta(\\mathcal{A})$ es el conjunto de distribuciones de probabilidad sobre el espacio de acciones $\\mathcal{A}$.\n",
        "\n",
        "## DM (Direct Method)\n",
        "\n",
        "La contribución individual de cada observación al estimador DM del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$ es:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\psi_i^{DM} = \\sum_a {\\pi (a|X_i) \\cdot \\hat{\\mu} (X_i,a)}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "donde $\\hat{\\mu} (X_i,a)$ es un estimador de la función de valor condicional \n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\mu (X_i,a) = \\mathbb{E}[R|X_i,A_i=a]\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Así, el estimador DM del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$ es:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\hat{V}_{DM}^{\\pi} \\, = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\psi_i^{DM} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\sum_a {\\pi (a|X_i) \\cdot \\hat{\\mu} (X_i,a)}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Supuestos:**  \n",
        "\n",
        "- $\\hat{\\mu}(X_i,a)$ está definido en el soporte de la política objetivo $\\pi$\n",
        "\n",
        "El sesgo del estimador DM del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$ es:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\begin{aligned}\n",
        "Bias_{DM} &= \\mathbb{E}[\\hat{V}_{DM}^{\\pi}] - V^{\\pi} \\\\\n",
        "&= \n",
        "\\mathbb{E}[\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\sum_a {\\pi (a|X_i) \\cdot \\hat{\\mu} (X_i,a)}] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&= \n",
        "\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\mathbb{E}[\\sum_a {\\pi (a|X_i) \\cdot \\hat{\\mu} (X_i,a)}] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&= \n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a {\\pi (a|X) \\cdot \\hat{\\mu} (X,a)}] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&= \n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a {\\pi (a|X) \\cdot (\\hat{\\mu} (X,a) - \\mu (X,a))}]\n",
        "\\end{aligned}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Así, el sesgo del estimador DM del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$ es cero si y solo si  \n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\hat{\\mu} (X,a) = \\mu (X,a)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "para todo $a$ en el soporte de la política objetivo $\\pi$.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## IPS (Inverse Propensity Score)\n",
        "\n",
        "Contribución individual por observación al estimador IPS del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\psi_i^{IPS} = \\frac{\\pi(A_i|X_i)}{b(A_i|X_i)} \\cdot R_i\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Estimador IPS del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\hat{V}_{IPS}^{\\pi} \\, = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\psi_i^{IPS}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Supuestos:**  \n",
        "\n",
        "- Positividad: $\\pi(a|x) > 0 \\implies b(a|x) > 0$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "El sesgo del estimador IPS del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$ es:\n",
        "\n",
        "\\begin{aligned}\n",
        "Bias_{IPS} &= \\mathbb{E}[\\hat{V}_{IPS}^{\\pi}] - V^{\\pi} \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\mathbb{E}[\\hat{V}_{IPS}^{\\pi}|X]] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\mathbb{E}[\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\frac{\\pi(A_i|X)}{b(A_i|X)} \\cdot R_i|X]] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\mathbb{E}[\\frac{\\pi(A_i|X)}{b(A_i|X)} \\cdot R_i|X]] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\mathbb{E}[\\frac{\\pi(A|X)}{b(A|X)} \\cdot R|X]] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a P(A=a|X) \\cdot \\mathbb{E}[\\frac{\\pi(A|X)}{b(A|X)} \\cdot R|X, A=a]] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a b(a|X) \\cdot \\frac{\\pi(a|X)}{b(a|X)} \\cdot \\mathbb{E}[R|X, A=a]] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&= 0\n",
        "\n",
        "\\end{aligned}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Si no se conoce $b$, y se estima como $\\hat{b}$, el sesgo del estimador IPS del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$ es:\n",
        "\n",
        "\\begin{aligned}\n",
        "Bias_{IPS} = ... &= \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a b(a|X) \\cdot \\frac{\\pi(a|X)}{\\hat{b}(a|X)} \\cdot \\mathbb{E}[R|X, A=a]] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\frac{b(a|X)}{\\hat{b}(a|X)} \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot (\\frac{b(a|X)}{\\hat{b}(a|X)} -1) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "\n",
        "\\end{aligned}\n",
        "\n",
        "con lo cual el sesgo del estimador IPS del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$ es cero si y solo si\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\frac{b(a|X)}{\\hat{b}(a|X)} = 1 \\iff \\hat{b}(a|X) = b(a|X) \n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "para todo $a$ en el soporte de la política objetivo $\\pi$.\n",
        "\n",
        "## SNIPS (Self-Normalized IPS)\n",
        "\n",
        "Contribución individual por observación al estimador SNIPS del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\psi_i^{SNIPS} = \\frac{W_i \\cdot R_i}{\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^{n} W_i} \n",
        " \\quad , \\quad W_i \\,= \\; \\frac{\\pi(A_i|X_i)}{b(A_i|X_i)}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "En este caso, el factor de normalización $\\frac{1}{n}$ se cancela en numerador y denominador, y por tanto, el estimador SNIPS del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$ es:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\hat{V}_{SNIPS}^{\\pi} \\, = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\psi_i^{SNIPS} = \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{n} W_i R_i}{\\sum_{i=1}^{n} W_i}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Supuestos:**  \n",
        "\n",
        "- Positividad: $\\pi(a|x) > 0 \\implies b(a|x) > 0$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "En tal caso, se cumple \n",
        "\n",
        "\\begin{aligned}\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}[\\frac{\\pi(A|X)}{b(A|X)} | X] &= \\sum_a P(A=a|X) \\cdot \\frac{\\pi(a|X)}{b(a|X)} \\\\\n",
        "&= \n",
        "\\sum_a b(a|X) \\cdot \\frac{\\pi(a|X)}{b(a|X)} \\\\\n",
        "&= \\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\\\ \n",
        "&= 1\n",
        "\\end{aligned}\n",
        "\n",
        "Por tanto,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}[\\frac{\\pi(A|X)}{b(A|X)}] = \\mathbb{E}_X[\\mathbb{E}[\\frac{\\pi(A|X)}{b(A|X)} | X]] = \\mathbb{E}_X[1] = 1\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Sin embargo, tanto numerador como denominador del estimador SNIPS son variables aleatorias correlacionadas, y por tanto, en general\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}[\\frac{\\sum_i W_i R_i}{\\sum_i W_i}] \\neq \\frac{\\mathbb{E}[\\sum_i W_i R_i]}{\\mathbb{E}[\\sum_i W_i]}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Además, como\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\begin{aligned}\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}[\\sum_i W_i R_i] &= n \\cdot \\mathbb{E}[\\frac{\\pi(A|X)}{b(A|X)} \\cdot R] \\\\\n",
        "&= \n",
        "n \\cdot \\mathbb{E}[\\psi^{IPS}] \\\\\n",
        "&= \n",
        "n \\cdot \\mathbb{E}[\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\psi_i^{IPS}] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "n \\cdot \\mathbb{E}[\\hat{V}_{IPS}^{\\pi}] \\\\ \n",
        "&=  \n",
        "n \\cdot V^{\\pi}\n",
        "\\end{aligned}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "y \\ $\\mathbb{E}[\\sum_i W_i] = n \\cdot \\mathbb{E}[\\frac{\\pi(A|X)}{b(A|X)}] = n$, en general se tiene que\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}[\\frac{\\sum_i W_i R_i}{\\sum_i W_i}] \\neq \\frac{\\mathbb{E}[\\sum_i W_i R_i]}{\\mathbb{E}[\\sum_i W_i]} = \\frac{n \\cdot V^{\\pi}}{n} = V^{\\pi}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Por la Ley Débil de los Grandes Números, el estimador SNIPS es consistente, pero en general sesgado:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} W_i R_i \\xrightarrow{p} V^{\\pi}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} W_i \\xrightarrow{p} 1\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "y como el cociente es una función continua, por el Teorema de Slutsky se tiene que\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\frac{\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} W_i R_i}{\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} W_i} \\xrightarrow{p} V^{\\pi}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "## DR (Doubly Robust)\n",
        "\n",
        "Contribución individual por observación al estimador DR del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\psi_i^{DR} = \\frac{\\pi(A_i|X_i)}{b(A_i|X_i)} \\cdot (R_i - \\hat{\\mu} (X_i,A_i)) \\, + \\, \\sum_a {\\pi (a|X_i) \\cdot \\hat{\\mu} (X_i,a)}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Estimador DR del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\hat{V}_{DR}^{\\pi} \\, = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\psi_i^{DR}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Supuestos:**  \n",
        "\n",
        "- $\\hat{\\mu}(X_i,a)$ está definido en el soporte de la política objetivo $\\pi$  \n",
        "- Positividad: $\\pi(a|x) > 0 \\implies b(a|x) > 0$\n",
        "\n",
        "Supuesto desconocido también $b(a|x)$, y estimado mediante $\\hat{b}(a|x)$, el sesgo del estimador DR del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$ es:\n",
        "\n",
        "\\begin{aligned}\n",
        "\n",
        "Bias_{DR} &= \\mathbb{E}[\\hat{V}_{DR}^{\\pi}] - V^{\\pi} \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\mathbb{E}[\\hat{V}_{DR}^{\\pi}|X]] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\mathbb{E} [\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\frac{\\pi(A_i|X)}{\\hat{b}(A_i|X)} \\cdot (R_i - \\hat{\\mu} (X,A_i)) + \\sum_a {\\pi (a|X) \\cdot \\hat{\\mu} (X,a)}|X]] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\mathbb{E} [\\frac{\\pi(A|X)}{\\hat{b}(A|X)} \\cdot (R - \\hat{\\mu} (X,A)) + \\sum_a {\\pi (a|X) \\cdot \\hat{\\mu} (X,a)}|X]] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a P(A=a|X) \\cdot \\frac{\\pi(a|X)}{\\hat{b}(a|X)} \\cdot\\mathbb{E} [ (R - \\hat{\\mu} (X,a))|X, A=a] + \\sum_a {\\pi (a|X) \\cdot \\hat{\\mu} (X,a)}] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\frac{b(a|X)}{\\hat{b}(a|X)} \\cdot (\\mu (X,a) - \\hat{\\mu} (X,a)) + \\sum_a {\\pi (a|X) \\cdot \\hat{\\mu} (X,a)}] - \\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\mu(X,a)] \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot \\frac{b(a|X)}{\\hat{b}(a|X)} \\cdot (\\mu (X,a) - \\hat{\\mu} (X,a)) + \\sum_a {\\pi (a|X) \\cdot (\\hat{\\mu} (X,a) - \\mu(X,a))}]  \\\\\n",
        "&=\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}_X[\\sum_a \\pi(a|X) \\cdot (1-\\frac{b(a|X)}{\\hat{b}(a|X)}) \\cdot (\\hat{\\mu} (X,a) - \\mu (X,a) ) ]  \\\\\n",
        "\n",
        "\\end{aligned}\n",
        "\n",
        "Así, el sesgo del estimador DR del valor de la política objetivo $\\pi$ es cero tanto si \n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\hat{\\mu} (x,a) = \\mu (x,a)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "para todo $a$ en el soporte de la política objetivo $\\pi$, como si \n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\hat{b}(a|x) = b(a|x)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "para todo $a$ en el soporte de la política objetivo $\\pi$. De ahí la propiedad de doble robustez."
